cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use drishti or reference its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "drishti: runtime failure detection and uncertainty quantification for robot policies"
abstract: >-
  drishti instruments a vision-language-action policy with forward hooks and scores three
  uncertainty signals at runtime — Mahalanobis distance on the proprioceptive state, random network
  distillation on the vision embedding, and the spread of the action head — then calibrates them
  against successful rollouts into a single conformal threshold. On an SO-101 pick-place task in
  MuJoCo it separates failed from successful rollouts at AUC 0.995 (n=60), catching every failure at
  a 17.6% false-alarm rate. The same detectors transfer to a Franka Panda in RLBench with per-task
  AUC 0.68-0.92. The repository also reports a negative result: a corrective VLM trained by GRPO
  over a VLA does not raise task success, because the VLA is effectively unsteerable by language
  (roughly 0.02 degrees of action change per joint under contradictory instructions).
type: software
